@* Written in each component, not in an _Imports.razor, whose class Razor makes public (ADR-0201).
   Every product using is written with global::. A component in ExSheet.Components would look a
   plain "ExSheet.Engine" up against the ExSheet component class first, and a plain "ExGrid.X"
   against sibling types (the CS0426 trap recorded in AGENTS.md). The Web namespace makes @on...
   handlers compile as event handlers rather than as plain HTML attributes. *@
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web
@using global::ExGrid
@using global::ExGrid.Cells
@using global::ExGrid.Chrome
@using global::ExGrid.Components
@using global::ExGrid.Keys
@using global::ExGrid.Selection
@using global::ExSheet.Engine
@using System.Globalization
@using System.Runtime.CompilerServices

@*
    ExSheet holds and computes; ExGrid paints, selects, navigates and reports (ADR-0046). This
    component renders exactly one ExGrid, as that grid's Consumer: it builds the Columns A … XFD,
    answers every Range Request from the Sheet, hands back a new row instance for every row the
    engine's SheetChange names and the same instance for every other row, and turns each Edit
    Intent into one engine step on the one undo stack (ADR-0048).

    What is deliberately not wired: ExGrid's sort and filter. They reorder a view of rows a
    Consumer owns, and a Sheet's rows are places (ADR-0046); OnSortChanged and OnFilterChanged are
    left without a delegate, and HeaderClickSelects gives the header click Excel's meaning.
    HideColumnMenu keeps the resize grips and drops the column-menu button: Excel's Headings
    carry no menu, and size to fit stays on a double-click of the edge (ADR-0050 item 12).
    HideCopyWithHeaders leaves copy with headers out, since a Sheet's column letters are addresses,
    not headers, unless the Consumer switches it on with AllowCopyWithHeaders (ADR-0048, ADR-0050
    item 13).
*@
@* One element around the Sheet, laid out as if it were not there (display: contents), so the
   browser's focus events reach ExSheet: while the Sheet is in a Pointing Scope, whether DOM focus is
   inside it decides whether it points (ADR-0058). Without a Scope nothing listens. *@
@* With the Sheet Toolbar shown (ADR-0100), the same element is the Sheet's box: the toolbar above,
   the grid below with what the toolbar leaves. The element is always there, so showing the toolbar
   never re-creates the grid. *@
@* It is also the Sheet's Input Root (ADR-0240 section 6, data-ex-input-root): the grid's key listener
   hears input on the whole Sheet from here, so the toolbar's keys and commands and the Sheet Tabs take
   their place in one order with the grid's own keys and presses. In a Scope it claims the keyboard
   crossing its edge (data-ex-claims, in _keyboardListeners). *@
<div class="ex-sheet" data-ex-input-root style="@FrameStyle" @attributes="_keyboardListeners">
@if (ShowToolbar)
{
    <SheetToolbar Context="_toolbar" Content="ToolbarContent" HeightPx="ToolbarPx" />
}
<ExGrid TRow="SheetRow" @ref="_grid"
        Window="_window" WindowStart="_windowStart" TotalCount="Sheet.RowCount" RowSequenceVersion="_sequence"
        Columns="_columns" OnColumnWidthChanged="_columnWidthChanged" HideColumnMenu="true"
        RowHeight="RowHeight" ViewportHeight="GridViewportHeight" ViewportWidth="ViewportWidth"
        PinnedColumnCount="PinnedColumnCount" Chrome="Chrome"
        OnRangeNeeded="OnRangeNeededAsync" OnEdit="OnEditAsync" SelectionChanged="_selectionChanged"
        CellType="SheetColumns.CellType" CellAlign="SheetColumns.CellAlign" EditorTextOf="SheetColumns.EditorText" FormulaBarBorrowedTextOf="SheetColumns.SpilledFormula"
        PaintedText="SheetColumns.PaintedText" CellAppearance="_cellAppearance" EdgeBorder="SheetAppearance.EdgeBorder" EditorAppearance="SheetAppearance.Editor"
        HeaderClickSelects="true" HideHeader="!ShowColumnHeadings"
        RowHeadings="(ShowRowHeadings ? RowLabels : null)"
        DataEdge="_dataEdge"
        ShowFormulaBar="ShowFormulaBar" NameBoxLabel="NameBoxLabelOf" NameBoxSizeLabel="NameBoxSizeOf" OnNameBoxEntered="OnNameBoxEnteredAsync"
        CompleteEditorText="_complete" PointAt="PointAtCaret" ReferenceText="_referenceText" CycleReference="CycleReferenceAt"
        OnPointStateChanged="_pointStateChanged" OnPointArrowFromOutside="_pointArrow"
        ReferencesIn="_references" OnReferenceKeyColoursChanged="_keyColoursChanged"
        ContextCommands="_contextCommands" CommandLabel="_commandLabel"
        PasteMaySpill="true" OnPaste="OnPasteAsync" OnPasteRefused="OnPasteRefused"
        CopyAnswer="_copyAnswer" OnCopyRefused="OnCopyRefused" HideCopyWithHeaders="!AllowCopyWithHeaders"
        ShowFillHandle="true" OnFill="OnFillAsync" OnClear="OnClearAsync" OnFind="_find"
        OnSummarize="_summarize" ShowSelectionSummary="ShowSelectionSummary" SummaryFigures="_summaryFigures.Shown" SummaryFiguresChanged="_summaryFiguresChanged" OnSelectionSummaryChanged="OnSelectionSummaryChanged"
        OnCopyRowsNeeded="_rowsNeeded"
        OnUndo="_undo" OnRedo="_redo" OnEditingChanged="_editingChanged" OnEditDiscarded="_editDiscarded" OnCommitRefused="_commitRefused" OnOverwriteNotice="_overwriteNotice"
        DeclaredKeys="DeclaredSheetKeys" OnDeclaredKey="_formatKey" OnBrowserTimeZone="_browserTimeZone" />
@* The Sheet Tabs (ADR-0331): one per Sheet of the Workbook, at the Sheet's foot, under the grid, as
   Excel draws them. A tab list to assistive technology, the selected tab its one tab stop. A press
   keeps the keyboard where it is, in the grid, and shows the Sheet; so do Ctrl+PageUp and
   Ctrl+PageDown, which the grid claims for the Sheet. Its height is the Formula Bar's, written inline
   (ADR-0028), and the Sheet's ViewportHeight includes it. A tab's press and the keys on the tab list
   take their place in the grid's Input Order (ADR-0240 section 6): each tab claims them (data-ex-claims),
   and a key typed straight after either acts on the Sheet it showed. *@
@if (ShowSheetTabs && _workbook is { } tabbedWorkbook)
{
    <div class="ex-sheet-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="@SheetWords.SheetTabsName" style="@SheetTabsStyle" @ref="_tabList"
         @onkeydown="OnSheetTabKeyAsync">
        @foreach (var tabSheet in tabbedWorkbook.Sheets)
        {
            var sheet = tabSheet;
            var selected = sheet == _sheet;
            <button type="button" role="tab" class="ex-sheet-tab" @ref="_tabs[sheet]" aria-selected="@(selected ? "true" : "false")" tabindex="@(selected ? "0" : "-1")"
                    data-ex-claims="@TabClaims" @onmousedown:preventDefault="true" @onclick="() => ShowSheetByUserAsync(sheet)">@sheet.Name</button>
        }
    </div>
}
@* Format Cells in a frame of the Chrome's own (ADR-0071, ADR-0010's note of 2026-09-30): beside the
   grid and outside its root, from the opening until OK or Cancel. Under the built-in Chrome it
   stands in the grid's popover frame instead (ADR-0050 item 16), and nothing is rendered here. *@
@* After OK or Cancel it stays until the keyboard has left it (FormatCellsContext.ReturnKeyboardFrom),
   so that the keys typed as the keyboard goes back reach the Sheet (decided with the user, 2026-10-13: they
   are held and handed on in order): one place in the markup, so the frame is the same instance. *@
@* A toolbar list hands its keyboard and held keys back before the next frame can take focus. *@
@if (!_formatCellsHandOffAfterToolbar && (_formatCellsFrame ?? _leavingFormatCellsFrame) is { } formatCellsFrame)
{
    @formatCellsFrame
}
@* What ExSheet has to tell the user — an address the Name Box cannot read, an operation the
   Sheet refused. The same element throughout, so a screen reader hears each change to it. A refusal
   the grid has already announced in its own live region, in the Sheet's words (ADR-0203), is shown
   here and hidden from assistive technology, so that it is said once. *@
<div class="ex-sheet-notice" role="status">@if (_noticeSaidByGrid) {<span aria-hidden="true">@_notice</span>} else {<text>@_notice</text>}</div>
@* ExSheet's stylesheet notice (ADR-0123, ERR-11), shown only by another version's stylesheet: last,
   so the toolbar and the grid stand where they always have. *@
<div data-ex-notice="stylesheet" data-ex-stylesheet="@NoticeStylesheet" data-ex-stamp="@NoticeStamp" style="display: none">@StylesheetNoticeWords</div>
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>Excel's default row height in ExGrid's geometry, and the Grid's own default: 28 px.</summary>
    public const double DefaultRowHeightPx = 28;

    // Rows beyond what the grid asked for, on either side, so that ordinary scrolling is
    // answered from rows already in hand.
    private const int ReadAhead = 50;
    private const int InitialRows = 100;

    private static readonly Func<int, string> RowLabels = static row => (row + 1).ToString(CultureInfo.InvariantCulture);

    // Point mode's two answers and F4's rewrite (ADR-0051) read only the text, the caret and the
    // range they are handed, so one instance of each serves every ExSheet.
    private static readonly Func<string, int, bool> PointAtCaret = SheetFormulaAids.PointAt;
    // The Reference Point writes: qualified with the Sheet shown's name while a Formula typed on another is
    // edited (ADR-0331 §5).
    private readonly Func<SelectionRange, string> _referenceText;
    private static readonly Func<string, int, int, EditorRewrite?> CycleReferenceAt = SheetFormulaAids.CycleReference;

    private static readonly Func<CellPosition, string?> NameBoxLabelOf =
        static focus => new CellAddress(focus.Row, focus.Column).ToString();

    // While a drag's button is down, Excel's Name Box shows the range's size, rows then
    // columns, and names the active cell again on release (ADR-0052).
    private static readonly Func<SelectionRange, string?> NameBoxSizeOf =
        static range => string.Create(CultureInfo.InvariantCulture, $"{range.RowCount}R x {range.ColumnCount}C");

    private readonly SheetHistory _history = new();

    // Every document this instance handed out. A Consumer that binds DocumentChanged back into
    // Document hands one of them in again, and that is the Sheet already open, not a
    // replacement: reopening it would clear the undo stack on every edit.
    private readonly ConditionalWeakTable<SheetDocument, object> _emitted = new();
    // The same for the Workbook Documents it handed out through WorkbookChanged.
    private readonly ConditionalWeakTable<WorkbookDocument, object> _emittedWorkbooks = new();

    private readonly Func<CellPosition, GridDirection, CellPosition> _dataEdge;
    private readonly Func<string, int, ValueTask<EditorCompletion?>> _complete;
    private Func<string, IReadOnlyList<EditorReference>> _references;
    private readonly EventCallback<IReadOnlyList<ReferenceKeyColour>> _keyColoursChanged;
    private readonly Func<ContextMenuContext<SheetRow>, IEnumerable<GridCommand>> _contextCommands;
    private readonly Func<string, string?> _commandLabel;
    // The Selection Summary's own words (a refused cell's reason), asked as a refusal's are (ADR-0203):
    // a substituted Chrome's, else CommandLabel and the Sheet's English.
    private readonly Func<string, string?> _summaryWords;
    private readonly Func<global::ExGrid.Clipboard.GridCopyRequest, global::ExGrid.Clipboard.GridCopyAnswer> _copyAnswer;
    private readonly Func<global::ExGrid.Finding.GridFindRequest, CancellationToken, Task<global::ExGrid.Finding.GridFindResult>> _find;
    // The Selection Summary (ADR-0130): answered from the Sheet's own cells, and the figures shown,
    // which this component holds as the grid's Consumer — so the figures menu works on every Sheet.
    private readonly Func<global::ExGrid.Summarizing.GridSummaryRequest, CancellationToken, Task<global::ExGrid.Summarizing.GridSummaryResult>> _summarize;
    private readonly EventCallback<global::ExGrid.Summarizing.SummaryFigures> _summaryFiguresChanged;
    private readonly global::ExGrid.Summarizing.HeldSummaryFigures _summaryFigures = new();
    private readonly Func<RowRange, CancellationToken, Task<IReadOnlyList<SheetRow>>> _rowsNeeded;
    private readonly EventCallback<GridSelection> _selectionChanged;
    private readonly EventCallback<string> _browserTimeZone;
    private readonly EventCallback _undo;
    private readonly EventCallback<ColumnWidthChange> _columnWidthChanged;
    private readonly EventCallback _redo;
    private readonly EventCallback<bool> _editingChanged;
    private readonly EventCallback<EditDiscardReason> _editDiscarded;
    private readonly EventCallback<GridCommitRefusal> _commitRefused;
    private readonly EventCallback<GridOverwriteNotice> _overwriteNotice;
    private readonly EventCallback<GridDeclaredKeyPress> _formatKey;
    private readonly Action<FormatCellsTab> _formatCellsTabShown;
    private readonly Func<Task> _returnKeyboard;
    private readonly Func<Task> _returnKeyboardFromFormatCells;
    private readonly Func<ElementReference, Func<IReadOnlyList<KeyboardEventArgs>>, Task> _returnKeyboardFromFormatCellsFrame;
    private readonly Func<Task> _formatCellsFromMenu;

    // Format Cells (ADR-0071): the tab it reopens on, this Sheet's own and Number at first (case
    // 22); the context while it is open; and the fragment of a Chrome that draws it in a frame of
    // its own, rendered beside the grid.
    private FormatCellsTab _formatCellsTab = FormatCellsTab.Number;
    private FormatCellsContext? _formatCells;
    private RenderFragment? _formatCellsFrame;
    // A Chrome's Format Cells frame that OK or Cancel ended, kept on the page until the keyboard has left
    // it: the element the keyboard leaves from, with the keys typed meanwhile, is in it.
    private RenderFragment? _leavingFormatCellsFrame;

    private ExGrid<SheetRow>? _grid;
    // The Sheet Toolbar's state, cascaded to its items (ADR-0100). Made once, as the component is.
    private SheetToolbarContext _toolbar = default!;
    private SheetColumnList _columns = SheetColumnList.Default;
    // Each cell's Font, Fill and Borders (ADR-0050 item 15, ADR-0071), read once per row for each
    // reading of the Sheet's formatting. A change that may reformat rows the engine does not name
    // starts a new reading, and the grid asks every painted row again (SheetAppearance.Lookup).
    private int _formatReading;
    private CellAppearanceOf<SheetRow> _cellAppearance = SheetAppearance.Lookup(0);
    // A resize of several whole columns the grid is still reporting, one column at a time: the
    // step that began it, and the columns not yet reported (ADR-0016, FN-12c).
    private (WorkbookStep First, HashSet<int> Pending)? _resizing;
    // The Workbook shown (ADR-0331), and the Sheet of it shown, which every part of this component
    // reads and edits: the grid draws one Sheet at a time.
    private global::ExSheet.Engine.Workbook? _workbook;
    private Sheet? _sheet;
    // What the grid showed of each Sheet when it was last shown — its Selection and scroll offsets
    // (ADR-0331 §1) — given back when its tab is selected again. A Sheet not yet shown has none.
    private readonly Dictionary<Sheet, global::ExGrid.Components.GridView> _views = [];
    private SheetEdges _edges = new();
    private SheetRow[] _window = [];
    private int _windowStart;
    private GridSelection _selection = GridSelection.Empty;
    // The Linked Table columns the Consumer was last told, so a change is told once (SH-31).
    private LinkedColumnColours _linkedColumnsTold = LinkedColumnColours.None;
    // What ExSheet has to tell the user. It stands until the user's own next action — an edit,
    // a paste, a command, a selection change — and a Consumer's Linked Table push, declaration
    // or new Sheet Document does not clear it: the user has not yet acted on what it says.
    private string? _notice;
    // A notice raised by a commit: the grid moves the Focus after the commit, as part of the
    // same gesture, and that move does not clear it.
    private bool _noticeOutlivesCommitMove;
    // A notice the grid has announced already — a refusal of a paste or a copy, in the Sheet's words
    // through the grid's label seam (ADR-0203): shown, and not said a second time.
    private bool _noticeSaidByGrid;
    // The copy this Sheet last wrote, recognised on a paste by its fields (ADR-0050 item 9).
    internal SheetOwnCopy? OwnCopy { get; private set; }
    // The engine's sentence for the copy refused last, for the notice the refusal raises.
    private string? _copyRefusal;
    private bool _initialised;
    private SheetDocument? _documentParameter;
    private WorkbookDocument? _workbookParameter;
    // Set when a new Sheet Document was opened in place of the one shown, until any edit open
    // over it has been discarded (ADR-0048).
    private bool _documentReplaced;
    // Whether the Sheet is hearing a write the grid raised — the commit of the edit being typed, or a
    // paste or fill — and whether another Sheet Document was opened while it was: that is the write's
    // own doing (the Consumer answered DocumentChanged with it). The edit the write ends was entered,
    // into the document it was typed in, so it is never said to be discarded, and no Overwrite Notice
    // that follows the write names a cell of a document no longer shown (ADR-0142, LV-32; ADR-0048).
    private bool _hearingWrite;
    private bool _documentOpenedUnderWrite;
    // The Row Sequence Version this Sheet hands its grid. A Sheet's rows are places, so its own edits,
    // inserts and deletes never move it (ADR-0046); it moves only when another Sheet Document is opened
    // in place of the one shown — one of the documents this instance handed out coming back is not
    // that — so that the grid drops the Selection, and refuses a paste, Delete or fill aimed at what
    // the old document painted rather than writing it into the new one at the same place (ADR-0011,
    // ADR-0142).
    private int _sequence;
    // ExSheet's own sentence for a discard it asked of the grid, said when the grid raises it.
    private string? _ownDiscard;
    private CultureInfo? _cultureParameter;

    /// <summary>Creates the component; the Sheet is opened when its parameters arrive.</summary>
    public ExSheet()
    {
        // Held in fields: a delegate's identity reaches the grid, and one made per render would
        // look like a change every time (ADR-0003).
        _dataEdge = FindEdge;
        InitialisePointing();
        // Answered synchronously from the engine, so the list shows in the render the keystroke
        // causes (ADR-0051). It reads this Sheet's Linked Tables, so it is the instance's own.
        _contextCommands = ContextCommandsFor;
        // Asked synchronously on both copy routes (ADR-0050 item 9).
        _copyAnswer = AnswerCopy;
        // Find over the Sheet's own cells (ADR-0055): answered from the engine at once, since the
        // Sheet is in hand; a step on another Row Sequence Version names nothing here: a Sheet's
        // rows never move (ADR-0046), and the version moves only when another document is opened.
        // Rows the grid reads outside the Window: a fill key's source row scrolled away
        // (ADR-0035). Every row is in hand, so the answer is whole and at once; a copy never asks
        // it, since CopyAnswer answers every copy (ADR-0050 item 9).
        _rowsNeeded = (range, _) =>
        {
            var sheet = CurrentSheet;
            var rows = new SheetRow[range.Count];
            for (var i = 0; i < rows.Length; i++) rows[i] = new SheetRow(sheet, range.Start + i);
            return Task.FromResult<IReadOnlyList<SheetRow>>(rows);
        };
        _find = (request, _) => Task.FromResult(request.RowSequenceVersion == _sequence && _sheet is { } sheet
            ? SheetFind.Step(sheet, request)
            : global::ExGrid.Finding.GridFindResult.NotFound);
        // The Consumer's wording first, then ExSheet's own English for its commands; null falls
        // back to the grid's built-in words for the grid's own commands (ADR-0036).
        _commandLabel = id => CommandLabel?.Invoke(id) ?? SheetCommandIds.EnglishFor(id);
        _summaryWords = id => Chrome?.Words(id) ?? _commandLabel(id);
        _summarize = (request, _) => Task.FromResult(request.RowSequenceVersion == _sequence && _sheet is { } sheet
            ? SheetSummary.Answer(sheet, request, at => SheetWords.SummaryRefused(at, sheet.GetValue(at)?.ToString() ?? "#VALUE!", _summaryWords))
            : new global::ExGrid.Summarizing.GridSummaryCells().Answer(request.Figures));
        _summaryFiguresChanged = new EventCallback<global::ExGrid.Summarizing.SummaryFigures>(null,
            (Func<global::ExGrid.Summarizing.SummaryFigures, Task>)(async figures =>
            {
                _summaryFigures.Choose(figures);
                StateHasChanged();
                await SummaryFiguresChanged.InvokeAsync(figures);
            }));
        _complete = (text, caret) => ValueTask.FromResult(_sheet is { } sheet ? SheetFormulaAids.Complete(sheet, text, caret) : null);
        // The References the grid colours and outlines while a Formula is edited (ADR-0057),
        // answered from the engine at once. It reads this Sheet's name, so it is the instance's own.
        _references = ReferencesOnSheetShown();
        _referenceText = range => _sheet is { } shown ? SheetFormulaAids.ReferenceText(range, shown, _editHome) : SheetFormulaAids.ReferenceText(range);
        // The grid tells the colour each Linked Table column's key was given; the Consumer is told
        // the columns (ADR-0057). No receiver: nothing on this Sheet changes for it.
        _keyColoursChanged = new EventCallback<IReadOnlyList<ReferenceKeyColour>>(null,
            (Func<IReadOnlyList<ReferenceKeyColour>, Task>)(keys => OnKeyColoursChangedAsync(keys)));
        // No receiver: a selection change re-renders the grid, not this component.
        _selectionChanged = new EventCallback<GridSelection>(null, (Func<GridSelection, Task>)(selection =>
        {
            // A formatting key adopts the Selection it carries, and a command the grid's, before
            // this notification lands on a circuit (OnFormatKeyAsync, AdoptGridSelection), so the
            // notification can name the Selection already held: that is no move.
            var moved = !selection.Equals(_selection);
            _selection = selection;
            RefreshToolbar();
            // Format Cells shows the Selection it opened over and sets what OK names on the
            // Selection: a Selection moved under it, by the Name Box or a Consumer, ends it.
            if (moved && _formatCells is not null) _ = InvokeAsync(EndFormatCellsAsync);
            // A selection change is the user's own action, and clears the notice — except the
            // move that completes the commit gesture whose refusal the notice reports, and a
            // Selection the grid dropped: no gesture of the user's empties it (ADR-0052), only
            // another Sheet Document opened under it (ADR-0011, ADR-0142), and the notice that
            // says so stands.
            if (selection.IsEmpty) { }
            else if (_noticeOutlivesCommitMove) _noticeOutlivesCommitMove = false;
            else if (_notice is not null)
            {
                ClearNotice();
                StateHasChanged();
            }
            return SelectionChanged.InvokeAsync(selection);
        }));
        // Ctrl+Z, Ctrl+Y and Ctrl+Shift+Z while no edit is open (ADR-0050 item 8, ADR-0048):
        // the same stack a Consumer walks with UndoAsync and RedoAsync, with a refusal said
        // rather than thrown into the grid's key handler. No receiver, as above: an undo
        // re-renders what its change names itself.
        _undo = new EventCallback(null, (Func<Task>)(() => StepByKeyAsync(UndoAsync)));
        _redo = new EventCallback(null, (Func<Task>)(() => StepByKeyAsync(RedoAsync)));
        // A resize is the user's, and the width is the document's (ADR-0046): it is recorded in
        // the Sheet as one step on the undo stack, and the column list follows the Sheet.
        _columnWidthChanged = new EventCallback<ColumnWidthChange>(null, (Func<ColumnWidthChange, Task>)(change => OnColumnWidthChangedAsync(change)));
        _browserTimeZone = new EventCallback<string>(null, (Func<string, Task>)(zone => OnBrowserTimeZoneAsync(zone)));
        // The grid says when an edit opens and ends, at the change and before the browser hears
        // of it (ADR-0050 section 6), so a command given in between is refused (ADR-0048). No
        // receiver: nothing this component paints depends on it.
        _editingChanged = new EventCallback<bool>(null, (Func<bool, Task>)(async open =>
        {
            IsEditing = open;
            // An edit ended while another Sheet than its own is shown — cancelled, or discarded — shows
            // its own again, where its cell is (ADR-0331 §5). A commit has shown it already (EnterAsync).
            if (!open) await ReturnToEditHomeAsync();
            // The toolbar greys out once the grid has answered the key or press that opened or
            // ended the edit, not inside that answer: drawn there, on a circuit, its render landed
            // among the keys and presses the grid holds behind the answer and lost what was typed
            // (layer 3, the Server host, SRV-5).
            if (ShowToolbar) _ = InvokeAsync(RefreshToolbarLaterAsync);
            await EditingChanged.InvokeAsync(open);
        }));
        // Typing thrown away is said, whoever discarded it: the grid, or ExSheet itself for a
        // replaced Sheet Document (ADR-0011, ADR-0048). No receiver: the notice renders itself.
        _editDiscarded = new EventCallback<EditDiscardReason>(null, (Func<EditDiscardReason, Task>)(reason =>
        {
            OnEditDiscarded(reason);
            return Task.CompletedTask;
        }));
        // A commit the grid refused because the row it was opened on is gone, or the rows moved
        // under it (ADR-0142, LV-20): the editor stands with the typing, and the notice says why.
        _commitRefused = new EventCallback<GridCommitRefusal>(null, (Func<GridCommitRefusal, Task>)(refusal =>
        {
            var address = new CellAddress(refusal.Cell.Row, refusal.Cell.Column).ToString();
            Tell(SheetWords.CommitRefused(address, refusal.Reason));
            StateHasChanged();
            return Task.CompletedTask;
        }));
        // A commit that landed over a cell that changed while it was being edited (ADR-0142, LV-11,
        // LV-21): the editor covered the cell, so the notice says what it replaced.
        _overwriteNotice = new EventCallback<GridOverwriteNotice>(null, (Func<GridOverwriteNotice, Task>)(notice =>
        {
            // Another Sheet Document was opened while the Sheet heard the write: the cell the notice
            // names is the old document's, no longer shown (ADR-0142, LV-32).
            if (_documentOpenedUnderWrite)
            {
                _documentOpenedUnderWrite = false;
                return Task.CompletedTask;
            }
            var address = new CellAddress(notice.Cell.Row, notice.Cell.Column).ToString();
            // Raised by the commit, so the move that completes the commit gesture leaves it standing,
            // as it leaves a refusal the commit raised (Tell).
            Tell(SheetWords.Overwritten(address, notice.SeenText, notice.ReplacedText), outlivesCommitMove: true);
            StateHasChanged();
            return Task.CompletedTask;
        }));
        // Excel's formatting keys, which the grid claims for this Sheet and raises with whether an
        // edit is open (ADR-0071, ADR-0050 item 14). No receiver: a format re-renders what its
        // change names, and a refusal renders its notice itself.
        _formatKey = new EventCallback<GridDeclaredKeyPress>(null, (Func<GridDeclaredKeyPress, Task>)(press => OnFormatKeyAsync(press)));
        // Format Cells (ADR-0071): the tab each opening reopens on, and the core's focus function a
        // Chrome whose frame lies outside the grid calls on closing (ADR-0021's note of 2026-09-30).
        _formatCellsTabShown = tab => _formatCellsTab = tab;
        _returnKeyboard = () => _grid?.ReturnKeyboardAsync() ?? Task.CompletedTask;
        // From a Chrome's Format Cells frame: the frame OK or Cancel ended goes once the keyboard is back.
        _returnKeyboardFromFormatCells = async () =>
        {
            await _returnKeyboard();
            LetFormatCellsFrameGo();
        };
        _returnKeyboardFromFormatCellsFrame = async (from, typedOnTheWay) =>
        {
            if (_grid is { } grid) await grid.ReturnKeyboardAsync(from, typedOnTheWay);
            else typedOnTheWay();
            LetFormatCellsFrameGo();
        };
        _formatCellsFromMenu = OpenFormatCellsByUserAsync;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// What a Wrapper cascades to the grid inside this component (ADR-0030): the glyph widths
    /// the grid resolves its Cell Metrics from, read here so that a column widened on entry is
    /// widened in the grid's own measure.
    /// </summary>
    [CascadingParameter] private GridPresentationDefaults? Presentation { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// The Sheet Document to show (ADR-0048). Handing over a different document replaces the
    /// Sheet and clears the undo stack, and an edit open over the Sheet it replaces is discarded,
    /// and said, rather than committed into the new one; handing back a document this component
    /// raised through <see cref="DocumentChanged"/> — as binding <c>Document</c> two ways does —
    /// changes nothing. Null is an empty Sheet in <see cref="Culture"/>.
    /// </summary>
    /// <exception cref="SheetDocumentException">The document's version is one the engine does not know.</exception>
    [Parameter] public SheetDocument? Document { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// The Workbook Document to show (ADR-0331): every Sheet behind a Sheet Tab, the one it records as
    /// shown in front. It acts as <see cref="Document"/> does — a different document replaces the
    /// Workbook and clears the undo stack, and one this component raised through
    /// <see cref="WorkbookChanged"/> changes nothing — and the two are not set together. Null, with
    /// <see cref="Document"/> null too, is a Workbook of one empty Sheet in <see cref="Culture"/>.
    /// </summary>
    /// <exception cref="InvalidOperationException">Both <see cref="Document"/> and this are set.</exception>
    /// <exception cref="SheetDocumentException">The document is one the engine does not read.</exception>
    [Parameter] public WorkbookDocument? Workbook { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// Raised after every change to the Workbook with its Workbook Document (ADR-0331): a change to any
    /// of its Sheets, and the Sheet shown, which the document records. The application persists it;
    /// ExSheet never does.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter] public EventCallback<WorkbookDocument> WorkbookChanged { get; set; }

    /// <summary>
    /// Whether the Sheet Tabs are shown at the foot of the Sheet (ADR-0331): on by default, as in
    /// Excel, with one tab for each Sheet of the Workbook. The Sheet's <see cref="ViewportHeight"/>
    /// includes them.
